{{also|Géraldine}}
==English==

===Etymology===
First used by the Earl of Surrey as a poetic name for Lady Elizabeth Fitzgerald,"one of the Fitzgeralds". Taken up as a given name in the 19th century, and used as a feminine form of [[Gerald]].

